The following example shows the use of the RESET pragma or directive with class variables and

methods. When you declare a variable in a class, it must be a public static variable in the class.
You can create the RESET pragma for the variable in a method of the class. You can also create

the RESET pragma after creating an object in the top function or sub-function of the HLS design.

 class bar {
 public:
  static int a; // class level static; must be public
  int a1;     // class-level non-static; must be public
  bar(...) {
  // #pragma reset does not work here for a or a1
  }
  // this is the function that is called in the top
  void run(...) {
